Strong Final Interview Answer

Snowflake Scripting extends SQL with procedural programming capabilities such as variables, loops, branching, cursors, result sets, and exception handling. It allows developers to build reusable stored procedures and complex ETL workflows directly inside Snowflake. Anonymous blocks are useful for temporary execution, while stored procedures provide reusable logic. Snowflake Scripting supports control-flow constructs like IF ELSE and FOR loops, making it suitable for automation, validation, and procedural data processing tasks.
